/-!
# Graph inputs for the paired extension of SL₃(2)

Every involution in the graph coset is conjugate to the chosen diagram
involution. Its fixed subgroup is S₃, and its fixed subgroup on the standard
Borel is generated by the highest-root involution.

The cocycle equation makes the matrix symmetric after coordinate reversal.
A kernel-checked table on its six binary entries supplies a conjugating
matrix. A change of basis transports the fixed group to the established
inverse-transpose SL₂(2) model. The eight standard upper matrices identify
its Borel intersection without enumerating the ambient group again.

These are the concrete single-factor inputs for the paired-group involution
and centralizer calculations in Aschbacher–Smith, Lemma 2.4.34, combined
manuscript of 1 March 2004, printed p.548.
-/

